   "evidence": "Line 159 defines `IsPosHomogeneous` via `c \u2022 a`, i.e. rescaling of the whole vector; bilinearity of `g : LinearMap.BilinForm \u211d V` (Basic.lean:386 `invariantMassSq g s = g s.sum s.sum`) gives `g (c \u2022 q) (c \u2022 q) = c ^ 2 * g q q`, so no scalar rescaling changes masslessness. The PR description itself says the intended schemes rescale \"the energy\" and \"the spatial part\", which the docstring omits.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Jets/Observable/Recombination.lean",
   "fix": "Say which part is rescaled, e.g. \"A scheme that rescales the energy (or the spatial part) of the merged pair so that the result is massless for a Minkowski form `g` ...\", which is what the `p` and `E\u2080` schemes do and is still positively homogeneous.",
   "issue": "Module docstring: \"A scheme that rescales a merged pair to make it massless for a Minkowski bilinear form `g` cannot be exact on all of `V`, but can be exact on the momenta with `g p p = 0`.\" A positive rescaling of the merged vector cannot make it massless: `g (c \u2022 q) (c \u2022 q) = c ^ 2 * g q q`, so scalar rescaling preserves `g q q = 0` and its sign. Read with the file's own `IsPosHomogeneous` (rescaling by `c : \u211d`), the sentence describes an impossible scheme, so the reader cannot connect `IsCollinearExactOn` to the `p`/`E\u2080` schemes it is intended for.",
   "line": 52
